# Bindgen LLVM-22-vs-23 compat expectation (issue #473).
#
# Each non-comment line names one Rust binding item the standalone
# `rust_bindgen` route (bindgen 0.72.1 prebuilt v0.0.2 with
# `--no-include-path-detection --formatter=none` plus the target compiler
# context from `pins.bzl`) must emit identically under the LLVM-22 parser
# baseline (hermetic-llvm 0.8.18, LLVM 22.1.8 via rules_rs v0.0.109) and the
# LLVM-23 target flags (hermetic-llvm 0.8.19, LLVM 23.1.0). The build-script
# route (explicit execution-platform libclang closure plus target parsing
# flags) must converge on the same set; divergence fails the compat proof.
# C source for every item lives in `bindgen.h` (checked by
# `//tools/ci:bindgen_qualification`); the Rust consumer links the native
# library separately in both routes. Unpinned LLVM is rejected.
DX_BINDGEN_MAX_LABELS
DxStatus
DX_STATUS_OK
DX_STATUS_EMPTY
DX_STATUS_BAD_ARG
DxPoint
DxTagged
DxMeasureFn
DxStore
dx_distance
dx_tagged_area
dx_store_create
dx_store_destroy
dx_store_len
dx_status_message
